  "description": "To investigate the relationship between genetic and transcriptional heterogeneity in a context of cancer progression, we devised a computational approach called HoneyBADGER to identify copy number variation and loss-of-heterozygosity in individual cells from single-cell RNA-sequencing data. By combining allele frequency and expression magnitude deviations, HoneyBADGER is able to infer the presence of subclone-specific alterations in individual cells and reconstruct subclonal architecture. Also HoneyBADGER to analyze single cells from a progressive multiple myeloma (MM) patient to identify major genetic subclones that exhibit distinct transcriptional signatures relevant to cancer progression.",
